 ## Push messaging
 
-- Token: request notification permission through the soft flow, then `getToken()`; send it to the backend with the
-  user id; update on `onTokenRefresh`; remove the mapping on sign-out.
+- Token: request notification permission through the soft flow, then `getToken()`; register it with the backend
+  for this app installation (for example `PUT /me/devices/{installationId}` with the token). The backend takes the
+  user from the verified ID token, never from a `userId` in the body. Update on `onTokenRefresh`; remove the mapping
+  on sign-out (`DELETE /me/devices/{installationId}`) before `auth.signOut()`. The unregister can fail offline; the
+  backend re-binds the installation when the next account registers, so do not block sign-out on it.
 - Delivery and display are separate: FCM delivers; when the app is in the foreground FCM does not show anything, so
   display it yourself (in-app banner, or Notifee if rich local notifications are needed; justify the extra package).
 - Handle all three entries: foreground (`onMessage`), background tap (`onNotificationOpenedApp`), cold start
